      "side": 1,
      "message": "i tried this patch on ruby. seems OK but i see a bunch of\n```\nI: power state 2 \u003d S5, in 0x061c\nBoot Time: 2, 914720100\nec:\u003e [914.812900 can\u0027t read any temp sensors!]\n...\n```\non `apshutdown`. that seems new with this patch.\nthis looks like it\u0027s from `thermal_control()`.\ndo we need to change the `CHIPSET_STATE_HARD_OFF` check\nto `CHIPSET_STATE_SOFT_OFF`?\nthat probably makes sense on x86, but i don\u0027t know if\nthat\u0027s always true.\n\nthe handler also sends a `EC_HOST_EVENT_THERMAL` to the AP\nafter that print in response - i kinda doubt this has a\nlistener in `CHIPSET_STATE_SOFT_OFF` even if the sensors\nare in some always-on power domain.\n\ni\u0027m not sure that we need to block this change on the sensor\nread fails but it does suggest we should take a closer look\nat `thermal_control()`.",
