      "side": 1,
      "message": "Estrange, ruby does not seem to use AP PWRSEQ driver enabled ([ruby/project.conf](https://source.chromium.org/chromiumos/chromiumos/codesearch/+/main:src/platform/ec/zephyr/program/fatcat/ruby/project.conf;l\u003d15?q\u003druby%2Fproject.conf\u0026ss\u003dchromiumos%2Fchromiumos%2Fcodesearch)), are you enabling it?\n\nSensors power signal is `PWR_RSMRST_PWRGD`, is powered up in G3 (or G3S5 for non driver) and is expected to be asserted in S5, so I would say that `CHIPSET_STATE_HARD_OFF` is OK.\n\nThis patch applies to only AP Power sequence driver to put power signals fully in sync with driver current power state, allowing the state handlers to set power signals based on events received.\n\nIs `RSMRST_PWRGD` enabled as shown in power signals bitfield `0x061c`?\n\nDoes this happen 100%? I wonder if another race condition between Thermistor refresh thread and AP Power sequence.",
